[17.411225, "o", "\r\n--- original_instruction.md ---\r\n"]
[17.41413, "o", "     1\t# Original instruction — the client's first message\r\r\n     2\t\r\r\n     3\tI am Delphine Marr. What follows is what I asked for to begin with, one entry per subject. The subject shown on each entry is the value the draft's `subject` column uses.\r\r\n     4\t\r\r\n     5\t## OI-201 `addressee`\r\r\n     6\t\r\r\n     7\tAddress the letter to the father's attorney.\r\r\n"]
[17.414527, "o", "     8\t\r\r\n     9\t## OI-202 `right_of_first_refusal`\r\r\n    10\t\r\r\n    11\tSay that Mr Adler — the father — agreed to a right of first refusal, and that the children are not to be left overnight without him present. Both the agreement and the overnight restriction must appear.\r\r\n    12\t\r\r\n    13\t## OI-203 `children_named`\r\r\n    14\t\r\r\n    15\tName both children with their ages: Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve. Both names and both ages are required.\r\r\n    16\t\r\r\n    17\t## OI-204 `overnight_stays`\r\r\n    18\t\r\r\n    19\tState that on several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away — both places must be mentioned, both children, and several occasions.\r\r\n    20\t\r\r\n    21\t## OI-205 `inconsistent_accounts`\r\r\n    22\t\r\r\n    23\tNote that the father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, a sitter to me, and his partner to the neighbours. All four audiences are required.\r\r\n    24\t\r\r\n    25\t## OI-206 `concern`\r\r\n  "]
[17.414853, "o", "  26\t\r\r\n    27\tSay I am concerned she may not appreciate that the stays violate the order or the position she has been put in — both limbs. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to concern.)\r\r\n    28\t\r\r\n    29\t## OI-207 `behavioural_plan`\r\r\n    30\t\r\r\n    31\tSay the behavioural plan is about confidence and stability and the stays have set it back — confidence, stability, and setback all required. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to behavioural_plan.)\r\r\n    32\t\r\r\n    33\t## OI-208 `request`\r\r\n    34\t\r\r\n    35\tAsk that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\r\n    36\t\r\r\n    37\t## OI-209 `enclosure`\r\r\n    38\t\r\r\n    39\tSay a certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\r\n    40\t\r\r\n    41\t## OI-210 `tone`\r\r\n    42\t\r\r\n    43\tKeep it soft, formal and succinct — all three. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to tone.)\r\r\n    44\t\r\r\n    45\t## OI-211 `sender_signature`\r\r\n    46\t\r\r\n    47\tSign it in my own name as Delphine Marr — the full name is r"]
[17.415077, "o", "equired; do not sign as counsel or on behalf of anyone else.\r\r\n"]
[17.415478, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32mappuser@7e206a420d13\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
[17.777167, "i", "printf '\\n--- clarification.md ---\\n'; nl -ba input/clarification.md\n"]
[17.778067, "o", "printf '\\n--- clarification.md ---\\n'; nl -ba input/clarification.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\r\n--- clarification.md ---\r\n"]
[17.781862, "o", "     1\t# Clarification — the client's later message\r\r\n     2\t\r\r\n     3\tWhat the client added afterwards, one entry per subject. The subject shown on each entry is the value the draft's `subject` column uses; any subject missing here is one the clarification leaves alone.\r\r\n     4\t\r\r\n     5\t## CL-301 `addressee`\r\r\n     6\t\r\r\n     7\tTo be clear: Adam is the father. The letter goes to Catherine's attorney — the mother's attorney — not to Adam's.\r\r\n     8\t\r\r\n     9\t## CL-302 `request`\r\r\n    10\t\r\r\n    11\tThe request stands: neither child overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\r\n    12\t\r\r\n    13\t## CL-303 `enclosure`\r\r\n    14\t\r\r\n    15\tYes, enclose the certified copy of the custodial plan.\r\r\n    16\t\r\r\n    17\t## CL-304 `salutation`\r\r\n    18\t\r\r\n    19\tOpen with Dear Counsel, since the attorney's name is still to be confirmed.\r\r\n    20\t\r\r\n    21\t## CL-305 `copies`\r\r\n    22\t\r\r\n"]
[17.781978, "o", "    23\tDo not copy anyone on it.\r\r\n    24\t\r\r\n    25\t## CL-306 `delivery`\r\r\n    26\t\r\r\n    27\tSend it by post to counsel's office.\r\r\n    28\t\r\r\n    29\t## CL-307 `tone`\r\r\n    30\t\r\r\n    31\tUse a firm, formal and brief tone — not soft, and not long-winded.\r\r\n    32\t\r\r\n    33\t## CL-308 `behavioural_plan`\r\r\n    34\t\r\r\n    35\tThe plan is about confidence, stability and peer relations. The stays have set back confidence only — not the whole plan.\r\r\n    36\t\r\r\n    37\t## CL-309 `concern`\r\r\n    38\t\r\r\n"]
[17.782208, "o", "    39\tI am concerned only about the position she has been put in. Do not raise whether she appreciates that the stays violate the order.\r\r\n"]
[17.783067, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32mappuser@7e206a420d13\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
[18.169009, "i", "printf '\\n--- submission_format.md ---\\n'; nl -ba input/submission_format.md\n"]
[18.169754, "o", "printf '\\n--- submission_format.md ---\\n'; nl -ba input/submission_format.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[18.169991, "o", "\r\n--- submission_format.md ---\r\n"]
[18.173111, "o", "     1\t# Submission format\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tDeliver exactly these files, in your working directory:\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\t- `answer.md` — The written review, carrying the number of letter lines at odds with the client's record\r\n     6\t- `letter_line_review.csv` — One row per line of the draft letter, giving its verdict and the record entry that governs it\r\n     7\t- `results.json` — a JSON object; see below.\r\n     8\t\r\n     9\t## `answer.md`\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t`answer.md` states `Letter lines at odds with the record: <count>` — the figure placed beside its label, in the very sentence that names the label (that sentence may appear anywhere in the review, including mid-paragraph). At least sixty words of prose that use the vocabulary of that required label (including the word `record`). Each figure stands beside its label once, stated as the finding — not offered as one of two candidates.\r\n    12\t\r\n"]
[18.174114, "o", "    13\t## `letter_line_review.csv`\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\tHeader, exactly: `line_id,verdict,record_entry`\r\n"]
[18.174705, "o", "    16\tOne row per record, keyed by `line_id`.\r\n    17\t`verdict` takes exactly one of: `VERIFIED`, `AT_ODDS`, `NOT_IN_RECORD`.\r\n    18\tThe lines of `input/letter_lines.csv` appear in their numbered order, one row apiece, each carrying the verdict and the governing entry (`OI-…` or `CL-…`; `NONE` when neither record speaks to the subject).\r\n    19\t\r\n    20\tExample (placeholder values):\r\n    21\t\r\n    22\t```\r\n    23\tline_id,verdict,record_entry\r\n    24\tST-100,VERIFIED,OI-200\r\n    25\t```\r\n    26\t\r\n    27\t## `results.json`\r\n    28\t\r\n    29\tA JSON object with exactly these keys and nothing else:\r\n    30\t\r\n    31\t- `verified_count` — number\r\n    32\t- `at_odds_count` — number\r\n    33\t- `not_in_record_count` — number\r\n    34\t- `clarification_governed_count` — number\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\tShape example (placeholder values):\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\t```json\r\n    39\t{\r\n    40\t  \"verified_count\": 0,\r\n    41\t  \"at_odds_count\": 0,\r\n    42\t  \"not_in_record_count\": 0,\r\n    43\t  \"clarification_governed_count\": 0\r\n    44\t}\r\n    "]
[18.174851, "o", "45\t```\r\n\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32mappuser@7e206a420d13\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
[18.592678, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv\nwith open('input/letter_lines.csv', newline='') as f:\n    rows=list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint('rows', len(rows))\nfor r in rows:\n    print(f\"{r['line_id']}|{r['subject']}|{r['position']}|{r['cited_entry']}|{r['wording']}\")\nPY\n"]
[18.593029, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
